# SHAPE-GATE.allow — this leg's exemptions from the shape gate (bench/tools/shapegate).
# The format, the rules and the shared tooling's entries: bench/SHAPE-GATE.allow.
# Paths are repository-relative.

names bench/tables/c/table_main.c 10 shape-blind leg: C has no template to pass the type through, so `TableMixed` is named where the storage is declared and at its Reset/Save/Load call sites, and `FixedTable`/`BenchMixed` likewise for the FIXED form's half (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §3.4), plus `BenchMixed` once at the read arm's packet storage typedef, the generated type its generated read/write are handed (BENCH-STANDARD.md §1.10, `bench_mixed_read`) — no field, no pinned value, no wire size (callsite)
